BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (Raspberry Pi hardware documentation \(selected chapters\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (Power supply) Tj T* () Tj T* (The power supply requirements differ by Raspberry Pi model. All models require a 5.1V supply,) Tj T* (but the current required generally increases according to model. All models up to the Raspberry) Tj T* (Pi 3 require a micro USB power connector, while Raspberry Pi 4, Raspberry Pi 400, and Raspberry) Tj T* (Pi 5 use a USB-C connector.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The current consumed by each Raspberry Pi depends on the peripherals connected.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Recommended power supplies) Tj T* () Tj T* (For Raspberry Pi 1, Raspberry Pi 2, and Raspberry Pi 3, we recommend the 2.5A micro USB supply.) Tj T* (For Raspberry Pi 4 and Raspberry Pi 400, we recommend the 3A USB-C Supply for Raspberry Pi 4.) Tj T* (For Raspberry Pi 5, we recommend the 27 W USB-C Power Supply.) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: No Raspberry Pi models support USB-PPS.) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: If you use a third-party USB-PD multi-port power supply, plugging an additional device) Tj T* (into the supply when your Raspberry Pi is connected causes a renegotiation between the supply) Tj T* (and the Raspberry Pi. If the Raspberry Pi is powered, this happens seamlessly. If the Raspberry) Tj T* (Pi is powered down, this renegotiation can cause the Raspberry Pi to boot.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Power over Ethernet \(PoE\) connector) Tj T* () Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 5 PoE header) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Ethernet jack on Raspberry Pi 5 is PoE+ capable, supporting the IEEE 802.3at-2009 PoE) Tj T* (standard.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Ethernet jack on Raspberry Pi 4B and 3B+ is PoE capable, supporting the IEEE 802.3af-2003) Tj T* (PoE standard.) Tj T* () Tj T* (All Raspberry Pi models with a PoE-capable Ethernet jack require a HAT to draw power through the) Tj T* (Ethernet port. For models that support PoE, we recommend the PoE HAT. For models that support) Tj T* (PoE+, we recommend the PoE+ HAT.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Typical power requirements) Tj T* () Tj T* (Product | Recommended PSU current capacity | Maximum total USB peripheral current draw | Typical) Tj T* (  bare-board active current consumption) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 1 Model A | 700mA | 500mA | 200mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 1 Model B | 1.2A | 500mA | 500mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 1 Model A+ | 700mA | 500mA | 180mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 1 Model B+ | 1.8A | 1.2A | 330mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 2 Model B | 1.8A | 1.2A | 350mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 3 Model B | 2.5A | 1.2A | 400mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 3 Model A+ | 2.5A | Limited by PSU, board, and connector ratings only. | 350mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ | 2.5A | 1.2A | 500mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 4 Model B | 3.0A | 1.2A | 600mA) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 5 | 5.0A | 1.6A \(600mA if using a 3A power supply\) | 800mA) Tj T* (Pi 400 | 3.0A | 1.2A | 800mA) Tj T* (Pi 500 | 5.0A | 1.6A \(600mA if using a 3A power supply\) | 800mA) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 1 of 16) Tj T* ET
