BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (Raspberry Pi hardware documentation \(selected chapters\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (Pi 500+ | 5.0A | 1.6A | 800mA \(with LEDs off and SSD inactive\)) Tj T* (Zero | 1.2A | Limited by PSU, board, and connector ratings only | 100mA) Tj T* (Zero W | 1.2A | Limited by PSU, board, and connector ratings only. | 150mA) Tj T* (Zero 2 W | 2A | Limited by PSU, board, and connector ratings only. | 350mA) Tj T* () Tj T* ([NOTE]) Tj T* () Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 5 provides 1.6 A of power to downstream USB peripherals when connected to a power) Tj T* (supply capable of 5 A at +5 V \(25 W\). When connected to any other compatible power supply,) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 5 restricts downstream USB devices to 600 mA of power.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The power requirements of a Raspberry Pi increase as you use its interfaces and attach) Tj T* (peripherals to it.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Most Raspberry Pi computers provide enough current to power standard USB devices such as) Tj T* (keyboards, mice, and basic adapters. However, high-demand devices — including modems, external) Tj T* (drives, and high-powered antennae — require additional power.) Tj T* () Tj T* (To check the current status of power output to the USB ports on your Raspberry Pi 5, run:) Tj T* () Tj T* ($ vcgencmd get_config usb_max_current_enable) Tj T* () Tj T* (Before connecting peripherals, check their power ratings and choose a power supply accordingly.) Tj T* (If you're unsure whether your power supply can deliver sufficient current, connect high-power) Tj T* (devices using an externally powered USB hub. For more information, see USB accessories.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The following table lists typical power requirements for common onboard interfaces and official) Tj T* (accessories:) Tj T* () Tj T* (Interface or peripheral | Typical current draw) Tj T* (GPIO pins \(combined\) | 50 mA maximum) Tj T* (GPIO pin \(individual\) | Up to 16 mA) Tj T* (HDMI port | 50 mA) Tj T* (Camera Module | 250 mA) Tj T* (Case fan | 60 mA at 5 V \(300 mW\)) Tj T* (USB keyboard or mouse | 100 mA to 1,000 mA) Tj T* () Tj T* (The following table describes the current \(in amps\) drawn by different Raspberry Pi models) Tj T* (across various workloads:) Tj T* () Tj T* (|  | Raspberry Pi 1B+ | Raspberry Pi 2B | Raspberry Pi 3B | Raspberry Pi Zero | Raspberry Pi 4B) Tj T* (Boot | Max | 0.26 | 0.40 | 0.75 | 0.20 | 0.85) Tj T* (| Avg | 0.22 | 0.22 | 0.35 | 0.15 | 0.7) Tj T* (Idle | Avg | 0.20 | 0.22 | 0.30 | 0.10 | 0.6) Tj T* (Video playback \(H.264\) | Max | 0.30 | 0.36 | 0.55 | 0.23 | 0.85) Tj T* (| Avg | 0.22 | 0.28 | 0.33 | 0.16 | 0.78) Tj T* (Stress | Max | 0.35 | 0.82 | 1.34 | 0.35 | 1.25) Tj T* (| Avg | 0.32 | 0.75 | 0.85 | 0.23 | 1.2) Tj T* (Halt current |  |  |  | 0.10 | 0.055 | 0.023) Tj T* () Tj T* ([NOTE]) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 2 of 16) Tj T* ET
