BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (Raspberry Pi hardware documentation \(selected chapters\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (Using revision codes for board identification) Tj T* () Tj T* (From the command line we can use the following to get the revision code of the board:) Tj T* () Tj T* ($ cat /proc/cpuinfo | grep Revision) Tj T* (Revision      : c03111) Tj T* () Tj T* (In this example above, we have a hexadecimal revision code of c03111. Converting this to binary,) Tj T* (we get 0 0 0 000 0 0 1 100 0000 0011 00010001 0001. Spaces have been inserted to show the) Tj T* (borders between each section of the revision code, according to the above table.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Starting from the lowest order bits, the bottom four \(0-3\) are the board revision number, so) Tj T* (this board has a revision of 1. The next eight bits \(4-11\) are the board type, in this case) Tj T* (binary 00010001, hex 11, so this is a Raspberry Pi 4B. Using the same process, we can determine) Tj T* (that the processor is a BCM2711, the board was manufactured by Sony UK, and it has 4 GB of RAM.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Getting the revision code in your program) Tj T* () Tj T* (Obviously there are so many programming languages out there it's not possible to give examples) Tj T* (for all of them, but here are two quick examples for C and Python. Both these examples use a) Tj T* (system call to run a bash command that gets the cpuinfo and pipes the result to awk to recover) Tj T* (the required revision code. They then use bit operations to extract the New, Model, and Memory) Tj T* (fields from the code.) Tj T* () Tj T* (#include <stdio.h> #include <stdlib.h>) Tj T* () Tj T* (int main\( int argc, char argv[] \) { FILE fp; char revcode[32];) Tj T* () Tj T* (fp = popen\("cat /proc/cpuinfo | awk '/Revision/ {print $3}'", "r"\);) Tj T* (if \(fp == NULL\)) Tj T* (exit\(1\);) Tj T* (fgets\(revcode, sizeof\(revcode\), fp\);) Tj T* (pclose\(fp\);) Tj T* () Tj T* (int code = strtol\(revcode, NULL, 16\); int new = \(code >> 23\) & 0x1; int model = \(code >> 4\) &) Tj T* (0xff; int mem = \(code >> 20\) & 0x7;) Tj T* () Tj T* (if \(new && model == 0x11 && mem >= 3\)  // Note, 3 in the mem field is 2 GB printf\("We are a 4B) Tj T* (with at least 2 GB of RAM!\\n" \);) Tj T* () Tj T* (return 0; }) Tj T* () Tj T* (And the same in Python:) Tj T* () Tj T* (import subprocess) Tj T* () Tj T* (cmd = "cat /proc/cpuinfo | awk '/Revision/ {print $3}'") Tj T* (revcode = subprocess.check_output\(cmd, shell=True\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (code = int\(revcode, 16\) new = \(code >> 23\) & 0x1 model = \(code >> 4\) & 0xff mem = \(code >> 20\) &) Tj T* (0x7) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 8 of 16) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
