s list contains the publicly available information on the registers. If a register or bit is) Tj T* (not defined here, then it is not public.) Tj T* () Tj T* (16:: OTP control register – BCM2711 + Bit 26: disables VC JTAG Bit 27: disables VC JTAG) Tj T* () Tj T* (17:: bootmode register + Bit 1: sets the oscillator frequency to 19.2 MHz Bit 3: enables pull) Tj T* (ups on the SDIO pins Bit 15: disables ROM RSA key 0 – \(secure boot enabled if set\) \(BCM2711\) Bit) Tj T* (19: enables GPIO bootmode Bit 20: sets the bank to check for GPIO bootmode Bit 21: enables) Tj T* (booting from SD card Bit 22: sets the bank to boot from Bit 28: enables USB device booting Bit) Tj T* (29: enables USB host booting \(ethernet and mass storage\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: On BCM2711 the bootmode is defined by the bootloader EEPROM configuration instead of OTP.) Tj T* () Tj T* (18:: copy of bootmode register 28:: serial number 29:: ~\(serial number\) 30:: revision code ^1^) Tj T* (33:: board revision extended – the meaning depends on the board model. This is available through) Tj T* (device-tree in /proc/device-tree/chosen/rpi-boardrev-ext and for testing purposes this OTP value) Tj T* (can be temporarily overridden by setting board_rev_ext in config.txt. + Compute Module 4 Bit 30:) Tj T* (Whether the Compute Module has a Wi-Fi module fitted 0 – Wi-Fi 1 – No Wi-Fi Bit 31: Whether the) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 10 of 16) Tj T* ET
