ull 64 bit serial number is available in /proc/device-) Tj T* (tree/serial-number) Tj T* () Tj T* (50-51:: Ethernet MAC address This is passed to the operating system in the Device Tree, for) Tj T* (example, /proc/device-tree/axi/pcie@120000/rp1/ethernet@100000/local-mac-address) Tj T* () Tj T* (52-53:: Wi-Fi MAC address This is passed to the operating system in the Device Tree, for) Tj T* (example, /proc/device-tree/axi/mmc@1100000/wifi@1/local-mac-address) Tj T* () Tj T* (54-55:: Bluetooth MAC address This is passed to the operating system in the Device Tree, for) Tj T* (example, /proc/device-tree/soc/serial@7d50c000/bluetooth/local-bd-address) Tj T* () Tj T* (77-84:: customer OTP values) Tj T* () Tj T* (86:: board country – The default keyboard country code used by piwiz If set, this is available) Tj T* (through Device Tree in /proc/device-tree/chosen/rpi-country-code) Tj T* () Tj T* (87-88:: customer Ethernet MAC address Overrides OTP rows 50-51 if set) Tj T* () Tj T* (89-90:: customer Wi-Fi MAC address Overrides OTP rows 52-53 if set) Tj T* () Tj T* (91-92:: customer Bluetooth MAC address Overrides OTP rows 54-55 if set) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 11 of 16) Tj T* ET
