BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (Raspberry Pi hardware documentation \(selected chapters\)) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Both of the Raspberry Pi 5 fan options plug into the four-pin JST-SH PWM fan connector located) Tj T* (in the upper right of the board between the 40-pin GPIO header and the USB 2.0 ports.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The fan connector pulls from the same current limit as USB peripherals.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The official case fan draws approximately 60 mA at 5 V \(300 mW\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (Given the extra cooling performance of the Active Cooler, we recommend it for customers who want) Tj T* (to overclock their Raspberry Pi 5.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The fan is scheduled to turn on and off based on the temperature of the SoC. The default) Tj T* (temperature mapping is as follows:) Tj T* () Tj T* (Less than 50°C: the fan doesn't spin at all \(0% speed\). 50°C: the fan turns on at a low speed) Tj T* (\(30% speed\). 60°C: the fan speed increases to a medium speed \(50% speed\). 67.5°C: the fan speed) Tj T* (increases to a high speed \(70% speed\). 75°C: the fan increases to full speed \(100% speed\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (Temperature decreases use the same mapping with a 5°C hysteresis; fan speed decreases when the) Tj T* (temperature drops to 5°C below each of the above thresholds.) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: The temperature, hysteresis and speed figures given above can be adjusted by using the) Tj T* (various fan_tempN, fan_tempN_hyst and fan_tempN_speed dtoverlay settings \(where N is 0, 1, 2 or) Tj T* (3\). See the overlays README for full details. For example, adding dtparam=fan_temp0=55000 to) Tj T* (/boot/firmware/config.txt will cause the fan to remain off until the Raspberry Pi 5's) Tj T* (temperature reaches 55°C.) Tj T* () Tj T* (At boot the fan is turned on, and the tachometer input is checked to see if the fan is spinning.) Tj T* (If it is, then the cooling_fan device tree overlay is enabled. This overlay is in) Tj T* (bcm2712-rpi-5-b.dtb by default, but with status=disabled.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 5 fan connector pinout) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Raspberry Pi 5 fan connector is a 1 mm pitch JST-SH socket containing the following four) Tj T* (pins:) Tj T* () Tj T* (Pin | Function | Wire colour) Tj T* (1 | +5V | Red) Tj T* (2 | PWM | Blue) Tj T* (3 | GND | Black) Tj T* (4 | Tach | Yellow) Tj T* () Tj T* (Real Time Clock \(RTC\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Raspberry Pi 5 includes an RTC module. This can be battery powered through the J5 \(BAT\)) Tj T* (connector on the board. When the components are facing up and the logo is in the correct) Tj T* (orientation, the J5 connector is located towards the near left corner of the board and to the) Tj T* (right of the USB-C power connector.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The J5 battery connector) Tj T* () Tj T* (You can set a wake alarm, which switches the board to a very low-power state \(approximately 3) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 14 of 16) Tj T* ET
