BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (Raspberry Pi hardware documentation \(selected chapters\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (mA\). When the alarm time is reached, the board powers back on. This can be useful for periodic) Tj T* (jobs like time-lapse imagery.) Tj T* () Tj T* (To support the low-power mode for wake alarms:) Tj T* () Tj T* (Edit the bootloader configuration. + $ sudo rpi-eeprom-config --edit) Tj T* () Tj T* (Add the following two lines. + POWER_OFF_ON_HALT=1 WAKE_ON_GPIO=0) Tj T* () Tj T* (You can test the functionality with:) Tj T* () Tj T* ($ echo +600 | sudo tee /sys/class/rtc/rtc0/wakealarm) Tj T* ($ sudo halt) Tj T* () Tj T* (This command halts the board into a very low-power state, then wakes and restarts after 10) Tj T* (minutes.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The RTC also provides the time on boot, for example, in dmesg, for use cases that lack access to) Tj T* (NTP:) Tj T* () Tj T* ([    1.295799] rpi-rtc soc:rpi_rtc: setting system clock to 2023-08-16T15:58:50 UTC \(1692201530\)) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: The RTC is still usable even when there's no backup battery attached to the J5 connector.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Add a backup battery) Tj T* () Tj T* (Lithium-manganese rechargeable RTC battery) Tj T* () Tj T* (The official battery part is a rechargeable lithium manganese coin cell, with a pre-fitted two-) Tj T* (pin JST-SH plug and an adhesive mounting pad. This is suitable for powering the RTC when the) Tj T* (main power supply for the board is disconnected. Since the current draw when powered down) Tj T* (measures in single-digit µA, the retention time measures in months.) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: We don't recommend using a primary \(non-rechargeable\) lithium cell for the RTC. The RTC) Tj T* (backup current consumption is higher than most dedicated RTC modules and results in a short) Tj T* (service life.) Tj T* () Tj T* (WARNING: Don't use a Lithium Ion cell for the RTC.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Enable battery charging) Tj T* () Tj T* (The RTC is equipped with a constant-current \(3 mA\) constant-voltage charger.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Charging of the battery is disabled by default. There are sysfs files that show the charging) Tj T* (voltage and limits:) Tj T* () Tj T* ($ grep . /sys/class/rtc/rtc0/charging_voltage) Tj T* () Tj T* (/sys/class/rtc/rtc0/charging_voltage:0 /sys/class/rtc/rtc0/charging_voltage_max:4400000) Tj T* (/sys/class/rtc/rtc0/charging_voltage_min:1300000) Tj T* () Tj T* (To charge the battery at a set voltage, add rtc_bbat_vchg to /boot/firmware/config.txt:) Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 15 of 16) Tj T* ET
endstream
