BT /F1 10 Tf 13 TL 50 800 Td (Raspberry Pi hardware documentation \(selected chapters\)) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (dtparam=rtc_bbat_vchg=3000000) Tj T* () Tj T* (Reboot with sudo reboot to use the new voltage setting. Check the sysfs files to ensure that the) Tj T* (charging voltage was correctly set.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Disable battery charging) Tj T* () Tj T* (To stop charging, remove any lines that contain rtc_bbat_vchg from config.txt.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Power button) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: This section only applies to Raspberry Pi models with a power button, such as the) Tj T* (Raspberry Pi 5.) Tj T* () Tj T* (When you plug your Raspberry Pi into power for the first time, it will automatically turn on and) Tj T* (boot into the operating system without having to push the button.) Tj T* () Tj T* (If you run Raspberry Pi Desktop, you can initiate a clean shutdown by briefly pressing the power) Tj T* (button. A window will appear asking whether you want to shutdown, reboot, or logout.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Select an option or press the power button again to initiate a clean shutdown.) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: If you run Raspberry Pi Desktop, you can press the power button twice in quick succession) Tj T* (to shut down. If you run Raspberry Pi OS Lite without a desktop, press the power button a single) Tj T* (time to initiate a shutdown.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Restart) Tj T* () Tj T* (If the Raspberry Pi board is turned off, but still connected to power, pressing the power button) Tj T* (restarts the board.) Tj T* () Tj T* (NOTE: Resetting the Power Management Integrated Circuit \(PMIC\) can also restart the board.) Tj T* (Connecting a HAT can reset the PMIC. Always disconnect your device from the power supply before) Tj T* (connecting a HAT.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Hard shutdown) Tj T* () Tj T* (To force a hard shutdown, press and hold the power button.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Add your own power button) Tj T* () Tj T* (The J2 jumper) Tj T* () Tj T* (The J2 jumper is located between the RTC battery connector and the board edge. This breakout) Tj T* (allows you to add your own power button to Raspberry Pi 5 by adding a Normally Open \(NO\)) Tj T* (momentary switch bridging the two pads. Briefly closing this switch will perform the same) Tj T* (actions as the onboard power button.) Tj T* () Tj T* () Tj T* (Page 16 of 16) Tj T* ET
endstream
